      "source": [
        "# Match the feature names with the trained coefficients\n",
        "list(zip(data.columns[:3].tolist(), model.coef_))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "732fa7a7",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "732fa7a7"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Question 2.3 (Interpreting model coefficients)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "- What is the trained linear regression model?\n",
        "\n",
        "- **(replace $\\beta_i$ below with the trained coefficients, reserve four decimal places, 5 pts)**\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{Sales} = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 \\times \\text{TV} + \\beta_2 \\times \\text{Radio} + \\beta_3 \\times \\text{Newspaper}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "- **(Open) question (5 pts)**: how do you interpret the coefficient of **TV** ($\\beta_1$)?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "4d3027a9",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4d3027a9"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Your solution for Question 2.3:\n",
        "\n",
        "The trained model is approximately\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{Sales}=2.9791+0.0447(\\text{TV})+0.1892(\\text{Radio})+0.0028(\\text{Newspaper}).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The TV coefficient is approximately $0.0447$. Holding Radio and Newspaper spending constant, an additional \\$1,000 spent on TV advertising is associated with an estimated increase of about $0.0447$ thousand sales, or about 44.7 items, on average. This describes the model's association, not necessarily a causal effect."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "198f14c2",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "198f14c2"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Making predictions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 10,
      "id": "86b4ded5",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T05:16:39.523554Z",
